// This is the plugin/bridge protocol flipped outbound: where BridgeService
// (core/plugin/proto/v2) lets kapi drive a plugin daemon, EngineService lets
// any gRPC-capable process drive kapi. Both speak the canonical content-model
// schema in core/proto/content/v1 (PartMessage and friends), and both reuse
// the same envelope patterns — a header-first client stream, chunked document
// bytes, and PartBatch framing to amortize per-message overhead.
//
// Transport and trust model: the service is served on a local Unix socket for
// trusted same-user peers only. There is no authentication in v1 — the socket
// mode (0700 directory) is the boundary, exactly like the plugin daemon
// sockets. Do not expose it on a network address.
